= Solution
{parent=3}

The hypothesis is possible only for $t\geq0$. For every $\lambda\in\sigma(x)\subset\mathbb R$,
$$
|t-\lambda|\leq\|t1-x\|\leq t,
$$
so $0\leq\lambda\leq2t$. The <spectral characterization of a positive element in a C-star algebra>[spectral characterization of a positive element in a C*-algebra] gives $x\geq0$.

= 4
{parent=5}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=4}

Positivity and $\|x\|\leq t$ give $\sigma(x)\subset[0,t]$. Hence
$$
\sigma(t1-x)\subset[0,t].
$$
The element $t1-x$ is hermitian, so its norm equals its spectral radius and is at most $t$.

